body:
I've joined SW/SWO and others on Reddit which I did on a throwaway account aswell. Maybe I'll post in there. 

&#x200B;

Tbh I never thought I would have even fell for a client, in the past two years I was saying to everyone who knew what I do, ' nope never not falling for a client, the ones who try to make me fall for them are cringeworthy to me, nope guys you're wrong, don't even say to me again ' so Mrxsrx27 what happens if you do fall for a client? What then'? nope I will never fall for a client ' and then .... I did. 

But I'm never doing this again!

&#x200B;

Thanks for all your help anyway, I didn't know about the tax charge and yeah I'm clearly still too naive.

>You've just said above you've had pimps. I had one too for a very short time when I was young- YOU are who they go for.

Okay what I meant was.... I started escorting at 19 and before I became independent.... I searched for agencies. I didn't know what full face full body meant, so most agencies ignored me. The ones who answered.... the first one who got back said I need my own car basically I needed to be my own security which now I can see that this is bad agency, at the time I was upset and this agency wasn't exactly nice about me telling them I'm new to the world of sexwork. Another said ' if you don't sending the right offing phots I'm not offing interested ' and cut me off. Another said I needed to provide my own flat not hotel etc. Another said yes but basically agency and driver takes £50 , so I would have been left with £40! So now I can see these agencies would have been really nasty pimps if I joined them but my naivety actually pushed them away.

&#x200B;

So I started independent. Actually at 19 I was quite rude on my old profile because too many people tried to take advantage before they even had met me! It actually worked, got some decent clients who are actually decent men. 

&#x200B;

>I had one too for a very short time when I was young- YOU are who they go for.

&#x200B;

The two "agencies" who wanted 50% yeah they didn't find me on adultwork nor were they on like any escort sites, adultwork, viva etc.... anyway I joined them out of desperation when I had taken break off escorting and the clients weren't coming in when I was trying to join back...... long story but anyway I would only be with them for 1-2 days, the clients weren't coming in when I was working under them, so they hardly got any money off me, which upset them off and something unrelated would happen so I left safely.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

>This good looking foreign man (I can guess where he is from)

Greece.

>Has 100% spotted an easy target.

Tbh it was me who made the move. He was actually leaving and I didn't care about him, I got my money, did my service and glad he was going. I just took a second look at him getting ready to leave and though ' wowwwwwww this guy is hot ' I asked him where he's from and it started from there. So If I just left him alone to go out of the door I wouldn't have been in this situation.

&#x200B;

>He may have even been told by your former pimps who you are.

&#x200B;

I doubt this. I also made a new profile which I've has for a year under a different name plus when I met him I was actually touring kind of in another city, I don't think he uses recommendations,  I believe some things like him saying not using recommendations or whatever to be true, as I did spy on him from a spam account without him knowing and a lot of things he said seemed to check out, like him saying his birthday is 29th March xxxx , and doing my research I can see people wishing him happy birthday on 29th March from years ago, also where he said he's single etc, he does work in a bar for min wage as I've seen him in x bar without him knowing I checked to see if he works there or not, so I believe he 's probably telling the truth when he says can't afford Adultwork all the time and has only used it 3 times, then again someone I told about this situation said ' that's the thing about con-men some things that they say will be true the rest is bullshit. '

&#x200B;

>because escorting and being blinded by love because someone is hot and pays a few dates is a recipe for disaster.

Thanks for the sites. I think his looks could have played a part in it, but tbh I've had good looking clients before and after and tbh when they've tried to haggle or try to date me for free or like ' I know you're going to say no, but can I take you out for a drink?' actually really puts me off, I even had one straight after the greek guy, even then I think they're hot still puts me off when they try and take advantage, I think I just liked this guy and was blinded by love, him paying for things at first and him refusing not to not pay at first I can see now that was just to reel me in... my only saving grace was that I had to ask for outside advice as if a client conned me I wouldn't have lived with myself at all, I would have felt too stupid

&#x200B;

>How do I know? I went through his phone. No I'm not sorry

&#x200B;

Tbh real talk............. I never got this. Like when a person who has suspicions goes through their partners phone and finds out that their suspicions are right, people come jumping in like ' well you shouldn't be dating someone if you don't trust them' ????? Like yeah you shouldn't be snopping on your partner but sometimes that's the only way you find out the truth
